    // bracket-or-paren scope so \`arr[i==0]\` doesn't trip the splitter.
    // Two guards: skip when the previous char is also \`=\`/\`!\` (we're in
    // the middle of a multi-char op token, not at its start), and skip
    // when the resulting lhs is whitespace-only (degenerate input like
    // \`{{ === }}\` should fall through to the missing-val placeholder
